  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "1 \u00b7 Ingest",
      "items": [
        "Three ways in: syslog UDP/TCP, POST /api/classify or /api/ingest, and the CLI (casewright <logfile>). SEED_LOG_FILE replays a demo log at start.",
        "Syslog lines go to a worker pool with TrySubmit. A slow LLM drops lines and counts them in metrics, so senders never block.",
        "The parser turns syslog/JSON lines into a LogEvent before classification."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "2 \u00b7 Classify (rules first)",
      "items": [
        "In-house Sigma engine runs first. On a rule hit in rules-first mode the LLM is skipped (LLMCallsSaved metric).",
        "No rule hit \u2192 OpenAI-compatible LLM (Gemini default, Ollama or OpenAI). LLM error + rule hit \u2192 the rule verdict is used, so the alert is not lost.",
        "LLM_PROVIDER=none runs rules only: unmatched events are stored as Unclassified."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "3 \u00b7 record(): one path for every event",
      "items": [
        "IOC watchlists enrich the event (in-memory hash maps; feeds refresh in the background).",
        "A matching suppression marks the event: it is stored but goes no further.",
        "The event is persisted, then correlated into an incident that shares IP, user or host within the window."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "4 \u00b7 Respond & investigate",
      "items": [
        "Playbooks propose actions on alert; containment and Slack go through webhooks only after a human approves.",
        "The AI investigator starts once per incident when it opens or escalates to P1/P2, not once per alert. Limited slots; busy \u2192 skipped and counted.",
        "Agent tools: AbuseIPDB, OTX, MITRE lookup, similar past events (Qdrant). Output streams over WebSocket and is saved as an incident note."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Security & trust",
      "items": [
        "Login: bcrypt local accounts, hashed session cookie (SameSite=Strict + X-Requested-With), or SIEM_API_KEYS (SHA-256, constant-time).",
        "Middleware: request ID, logging, panic recovery, per-IP rate limit (login 1 rps), security headers, CORS, audit trail, role checks for admin routes.",
        "?api_key= is accepted only on WebSocket upgrades, because browsers cannot set headers there."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Storage & degradation",
      "items": [
        "POSTGRES_DSN set: events, incidents, actions, users, suppressions and IOCs share one pool; unreachable DB is fatal. Unset: memory stores, lost on restart.",
        "Qdrant down at start \u2192 semantic search and the similar-events tool are turned off; everything else runs.",
        "Retention (Postgres only) is off by default and purges only resolved incidents. /metrics exposes Prometheus counters."
      ]
    }
  ]
